    "https://www.umsl.edu/services/hrs/careers/student-employment.html": {
      "title": "Student Employment",
      "description": "Student Employment | UMSL Skip to Main Content University of Missouri–St. Louis Apply Request Info Give Human Resources About HR About Us HR Partners by Unit Staff Directory Careers at UMSL Careers Home Faculty Staff Students Employee Resources Employee Engagement Total Rewards Total Rewards Home Benefits Compensation Retirees Association University Holidays and Leave Wellness Managers Managers Home HR Processes and Forms Employee Relations Justification Learning and Development Performance Management Recruiting and Hiring Remote Work myHR Current Page: Student Employment Human Resources About HR About Us HR Partners by Unit Staff Directory Careers at UMSL Careers Home Faculty Staff Students Employee Resources Employee Engagement Total Rewards Total Rewards Home Benefits Compensation Retirees Association University Holidays and Leave Wellness Managers Managers Home HR Processes and Forms Employee Relations Justification Learning and Development Performance Management Recruiting and Hiring Remote Work myHR Student Employment Human Resources Careers Student Employment Student Employment Opportunities Learn more about Student Employment Opportunities with Career Services. I-9 Processing Students are not eligible to work until their preboarding and I-9s are complete. Students must submit their I-9 documents to Human Resources or NER before they can begin working. Steps Required for Students Step 1: Apply for Campus Jobs Looking for An On-Campus Job To look for jobs, check out Career Services On Campus Jobs webpage. Career Services is available if you need assistance with your resume or interviewing skills. Access MyGateway/MyConnect to schedule an appointment with the Career Services member in your Student Success Network. Additional Questions If you have additional questions about the hiring process, or would like assistance, please contact UMSL Career Services at the following: Phone Number: 314-516-5111 Email: careerservices@umsl.edu If you have additional questions about Federal Work Study, or would like assistance, please contact Student Financial Services at the following: Phone Number: 314-516-5526 Email: financialaid@umsl.edu Step 2: Preboarding and I-9s Congrats! You've done it! Now it's time to complete your Preboarding and I-9. To learn more about this process, download our Employee Registration guide to learn more about Preboarding and the I-9. At UMSL, we complete the I-9 document verification process online. You can find more information about this process on our designated I-9 webpage . If you have any questions about this process, please reach out to umslhr@umsl.edu Student Hours Federal Work Study A student can only work a total of 20 hours per week, even if they hold more than one student employment position. In some cases, students can work up to 28 hours per week.  A written agreement must first be obtained from the supervisor. During the summer, fall break, winter break and spring break, students can work up to 40 hours per week. See below (from HR 101 Employee Status ) for more information. Student Employees: A University employee that is enrolled as a student at the University of Missouri and whose primary association with the University is related to the pursuit of an academic program. Because academic pursuit is the primary purpose of the student role, Student Employees should not be scheduled to work more than an average of 28 hours per week across all concurrent University jobs during the measurement period [1] and should be in a student title as described in HR-204 Student Position Titles. **Students cannot work during scheduled class sessions. Federal Work Study The Federal Work-Study (FWS) program is designed to help undergraduate and graduate students who demonstrate financial need by providing meaningful employment that can help to offset educational expenses. The Office of Student Financial Services assists qualifying students find a part-time position on campus or off campus at an approved community service site.  Please review the Federal Work Study Handbook . Student Eligibility for Federal Work Study: You must meet all of the following criteria - You must complete your FAFSA for the application year. You must turn in any documents required by the Office of Student Financial Services . You must maintain at least a 2.0 GPA for undergraduate students, and a 3.0 GPA for graduate students. You must be enrolled at least half-time (6 hours/semester for undergraduates, 5 hours/semester for graduate students) in a degree or certificate program. You must be offered Federal Work Study. You can access this information in MyView to see if FWs is included in your financial aid package. You must attend the online mandatory work-study orientation session.* As a reminder - Priority is given to students already participating in the FWS program. Funding for the FWS program is very limited. New hire applications are processed on a first-come, first-served basis. The Federal Work Study application is usually available in early April preceding the start of the academic year. To learn more about Federal Work Study, please review the Office of Student Financial Services study guide on Federal Work Study.for more information about when the application will be made available each year. To apply for a position, you must have been awarded Federal Work Study and be registered to attend a work-study orientation session. For more information about Federal Work Study, please connect with Student Financial Services . To look at jobs, check out Career Services On Campus Student Jobs webpage to search for FWS jobs. * Student work-study session are online only. Federal Work Study Application: The Federal Work-Study (FWS) Application is now online. Please apply below: Federal Work Study Application Office of Human Resources 1 University Blvd.,  308 Woods Hall\n        \t\t\t\t\t\t\t        \t\t\t\t\t\t\t        \t\t\t\t\t\t\t    St. Louis, MO 63121-4400 Office Number: (314) 516-5805 Admissions Toll-Free: 1-888-GO-2-UMSL © The Curators of the University of Missouri | Accessibility | DMCA Policy | Privacy Policy | Careers at UMSL UMSL is an equal opportunity employer. For more information, visit our UMSL Statement of Nondiscrimination. University of Missouri–St. Louis Apply Request Info Give Admissions Visit UMSL Admissions Financial Aid Residential Life New Student Programs Advanced Credit Program Academics Majors and Degrees Research Colleges and Schools Libraries Course Schedule Online Programs Advanced Workforce Center Campus Life Student Involvement Veterans Center Career Services Health, Counseling, Disability Access Student Organizations UMSL Bookstore Community Bridge Centers and Institutes Community Engagement Event Services Touhill Performing Arts Center About UMSL About the University Chancellor Campus Safety UMSL Daily Transform UMSL Athletics Triton Athletics Full Athletics Schedule Tickets Athletic Facility Directions Louie's Locker Current Students Faculty and Staff Campus Calendar Directories A to Z Alumni Maps Careers at UMSL"
    },
    "https://www.umsl.edu/career-services/": {
      "title": "Welcome to UMSL Career Services!",
      "description": "Career Services | UMSL Skip to Main Content University of Missouri–St. Louis Apply Request Info Give Career Services Handshake Career Fairs and Events Upcoming Career Fair Prepare for a Career Fair Employer Career Fair Information Students Book an Appointment Career Fair Information Career Resources Prepare for a Career Fair Student Campus Jobs Alumni Employers Employer Information Employer Policies and Guidelines Employer Career Fair Information About Us About Career Services Policies Outcomes Staff Directory Current Page: Career Services Career Services Handshake Career Fairs and Events Upcoming Career Fair Prepare for a Career Fair Employer Career Fair Information Students Book an Appointment Career Fair Information Career Resources Prepare for a Career Fair Student Campus Jobs Alumni Employers Employer Information Employer Policies and Guidelines Employer Career Fair Information About Us About Career Services Policies Outcomes Staff Directory Welcome to UMSL Career Services! Career Services Upcoming Career Services Events UMSL Fall Internship and Job Fair 2026 UMSL Fall Internship & Job Fair 2026 Friday, September 11, 2026 | 9:30am – 1:00pm Touhill Performing Arts Center This campus-wide, in-person event is ONLY for UMSL students and alumni from all academic programs and levels. Discuss internship and job opportunities and connect and network with employers! REGISTER FOR THE FAIR! Students Register Through Handshake TODAY! Note: Employers registering to participate daily! Be sure to check back on the list of employers on a regular basis! Ace the Career Fair Workshops Ace the Caree r Fair Confidence Starts Here: Get Prepared, Make Connections, Succeed UMSL Career Services is hosting the UMSL Fall Internship & Job Fair 2026 on Friday, September 11, 2026. These sessions will give tips on how to successfully navigate the career fair. Register for the workshops below: In Person: 278 MSC, Career Services Suite September 3rd @ 3:30pm September 9th @ 3:30pm Virtual Zoom: September 2nd @ 3:30pm September 8th @ 3:30pm See your confirmation email from Handshake, click Event Details to access Zoom link. World Wide Technology Career Launch Day Tuesday, September 8, 2026 | 9:30 a.m. - 2 p.m. | MSC, The Chambers Build confidence with resume reviews, LinkedIn & career fair tips, and insights into World Wide Technology internships & early career opportunities. All majors welcome! Lunch provided. Register here. Connect with us The Office of Career Services is located in the Millennium Student Center, Room 278. Office Hours: Monday-Friday: 8am-5pm Students Finding a career is a major part of your degree journey. That's why we equip you with the resources and guidance to land your dream job. From career counseling and skill development to internship and job search assistance, we offer comprehensive support to help you succeed. Visit us to explore your options and connect with top employers! Find an on-campus job Book an Appointment Start your career Handshake is a meeting place where you and potential employers can connect. You can find internships, networking events, and target specific employers. In addition to the Handshake platform, UMSL career fairs offer you direct access to employers seeking talented individuals like you. Handshake Career Fair Career Resources Empower your job search with a wealth of resources designed to guide you to success. Find Career Resources Employers See how we can partner with you to build the future workforce you need. Information for Employers Faculty and Staff Find resources and support to guide your students towards successful careers. Information for Faculty and Staff Upcoming Career Events See the full career services calendar Connect with Career Services Career Services 1 University Blvd.  278 Millennium Student Center\n        \t\t\t\t\t\t\t        \t\t\t\t\t\t\t        \t\t\t\t\t\t\t    St. Louis, MO 63121-4400 Office Number: (314) 516-5111 Admissions Toll-Free: 1-888-GO-2-UMSL Email Address: careerservices@umsl.edu © The Curators of the University of Missouri | Accessibility | DMCA Policy | Privacy Policy | Careers at UMSL UMSL is an equal opportunity employer. For more information, visit our UMSL Statement of Nondiscrimination. University of Missouri–St. Louis Apply Request Info Give Admissions Visit UMSL Admissions Financial Aid Residential Life New Student Programs Advanced Credit Program Academics Majors and Degrees Research Colleges and Schools Libraries Course Schedule Online Programs Advanced Workforce Center Campus Life Student Involvement Veterans Center Career Services Health, Counseling, Disability Access Student Organizations UMSL Bookstore Community Bridge Centers and Institutes Community Engagement Event Services Touhill Performing Arts Center About UMSL About the University Chancellor Campus Safety UMSL Daily Transform UMSL Athletics Triton Athletics Full Athletics Schedule Tickets Athletic Facility Directions Louie's Locker Current Students Faculty and Staff Campus Calendar Directories A to Z Alumni Maps Careers at UMSL"
